==English==
{{was wotd|2025|March|29}}

===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*kelh₂-}}
Borrowed from {{bor|en|fr|calamiteux|t=calamitous}} + [[w:English language|English]] {{m|en|-ous|pos={{glossary|suffix}} forming {{glossary|adjective}}s denoting presence of a quality in any degree, typically an abundance}}. {{m|fr||Calamiteux}} is derived from {{der|en|la|calamitōsus|t=destructive, disastrous, ruinous, calamitous}}, a {{glossary|contraction}} of {{m|la|calamitātōsus}}, from {{m|la|calamitātem}} + {{m|la|-ōsus|pos=suffix meaning ‘full of; prone to’ forming adjectives from {{glossary|noun}}s}};<ref>{{R:OED Online|pos=adj|id=5673450220|date=December 2024}}</ref><ref>{{R:Dictionary.com|pos=adj}}</ref> {{m|la||calamitātem}} is the {{glossary|accusative}} {{glossary|singular}} of {{m|la|calamitās|t=disaster, misfortune, calamity; damage, harm; loss}}, from {{m|la|*calamis|t=damaged}} (ultimately from {{der|en|ine-pro|*kelh₂-|t=to beat; to break}}) + {{m|la|-tās|pos=suffix forming {{glossary|abstract noun}}s denoting a condition or state}}. {{surf|en|calamity|-ous}}.

